[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Parser-only input qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-QUAL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Evidence-gated valid sample acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
The sample acceptance gate shall require an actual completed result for every declared inventory row and acceptance for every valid sample under an identified input profile. Non-deck documents and malformed syntax fixtures may have explicit source-evidenced dispositions pinned to input SHA-256 and expected outcome. Legacy-byte samples shall require acceptance in an explicit byte-preserving replay while retaining strict UTF-8 negative outcomes. Unexplained grammar gaps, timeouts, missing input and resource refusals shall remain outstanding.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-PREDICT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Full recognition fallback and differential evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
An optional ANTLR SLL first pass shall use bail-on-error recognition and require complete input consumption. A failed first pass shall be discarded and retried with full LL recognition and fresh diagnostics and recursion accounting. LL-only operation shall remain selectable for differential tests. Neither prediction strategy shall invoke elaboration or simulation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-LEX-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Context-specific lexical recognition
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall recognize signed, hyphenated, numeric-prefixed, Unicode and bus node spellings, library paths, and continuation records across comments, while retaining distinct braced-expression tokenization and XSPICE vector delimiters. It shall accept the optional equals delimiter in function definitions and preserve behavioral-source parameter assignments after an expression. It shall preserve source spelling and reject malformed expression delimiters and missing operands.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-DEV-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Additional device and numerical-model syntax families
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall recognize OSDI N, CPL P, TXL Y and URC U instance structure, model references and parameter tails without loading their implementations. It shall recognize numerical-model continuation comments, negated CIDER flags and complex parameter pairs. It shall preserve PSpice U-card logic/delay structure and leading-apostrophe digital constants without altering ordinary closed quoted expressions on subsequent cards. It shall recognize three-terminal VDMOS syntax and legacy model outer parentheses as separators while keeping expression, call and connection delimiters strict. Model-dependent terminal counts and physical parameter validation shall remain elaboration concerns.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-SCRIPT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit inert ngspice command-file mode
STATEMENT: >>>
An explicit ng_script title marker shall select the generated command-file grammar and retain command records without execution. This shall not relax block closure for ordinary titled decks. Command-file structural acceptance shall be identified separately from detailed command-language validation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Reference: ngspice src/frontend/inp.c and inpcom.c distinguish command files by the ng_script marker. Verification: CommonSyntaxTests and corpus InputKind metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-PROFILE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit reproducible input and resource profiles
STATEMENT: >>>
Sample campaigns shall expose validated byte, token, worker-duration, total-duration and concurrency limits and record actual settings. UTF-8 decoding shall remain strict by default; a separately declared legacy-byte profile may use lossless Latin-1 mapping and shall identify that interpretation per input rather than silently repairing invalid UTF-8. Interactive default allocation bounds shall remain unchanged when expanded campaign bounds are selected.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Generated recognition and solver independence
STATEMENT: >>>
The parser-only frontend shall use a pinned established lexer/parser generator and produce source-located syntax without invoking numerical simulation, model resolution, include loading or control commands. Unknown grammar extensions shall be identified separately from recognized syntax.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design: docs/parser-only-plan.md. Implementation and evidence are recorded in docs/parser-only-results.md; Draft does not assert complete ngspice conformance.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Complete inventory attempts and honest acceptance levels
STATEMENT: >>>
The parser-only campaign shall attempt every row of the selected ngspice sample inventory and tracked repository SPICE samples. It shall retain input and grammar provenance and distinguish structural acceptance, grammar gaps, syntax rejection, invalid encoding, missing input, timeout and budget exhaustion. Structural acceptance shall not assert full device-parameter validation or simulation support.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-XSPICE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Inert code-model instance grammar
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated grammar shall recognize A-device model references and scalar, vector, differential, inverted, null and explicitly typed XSPICE connections, including user-defined connection type names. It shall reject malformed connection delimiters and differential parenthesized pairs with other than two nodes, without loading code models or resolving their port contracts.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Primary syntax: ngspice manual, Code Model Element and .MODEL Cards; src/xspice/mif/mif_inp2.c and mifutil.c at the pinned ngspice corpus revision. Implementation: SpiceLexer.g4 and SpiceParser.g4 xspice/xport/xpair/xvector. Verification: XspiceTests.cs, replay 481,20261031, and parser-only corpus evidence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Malformed input and resource bounds
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall reject malformed delimiters and declared device-family minimum arities, preserve original physical source locations through continuations, and bound input bytes, recursive grammar forms including subcircuits and unary chains, diagnostics and worker duration. Regression and reproducible randomized tests shall challenge these contracts.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Actual corpus and executable provenance
STATEMENT: >>>
The parser-only campaign shall record the actual corpus checkout revision separately from the inventory's declared revision and retain executable hashes. It shall not report qualification completion if source or executable bytes change during execution.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-LEX-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded separator recognition
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated lexer shall consume runs of blank and comment-only separators without repeatedly rescanning their suffix for continuations. A 100000-blank-line input within the character profile shall complete recognition. The token-budget test shall use actual token-producing records independently of separator coalescing.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: SpiceLexer.g4 NL and CONTINUATION. Verification: BoundaryTests.Input_and_token_bounds_report_reasons. This finite regression is not a general worst-case complexity proof.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: NGC-PARSE-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-REF-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Punctuated node names inside voltage-reference expressions
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall distinguish node arguments of voltage-reference calls from ordinary arithmetic identifier expressions under the selected dialect profile. It shall preserve spellings such as V(VC+,VC-), V(REF+,REF-) and V(IN1+,IN1-) when nested inside behavioral expressions, without treating trailing node punctuation as a missing arithmetic operand. Malformed reference delimiters and malformed surrounding arithmetic shall remain rejected. Syntax acceptance shall not imply behavioral-source evaluation or numerical model support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Bounded implementation: generated VOLTAGE_REFERENCE mode and voltageReference production; FeatureExtraction observations and nesting guard. Verification: VoltageReferenceTests, including source ranges, ordinary arithmetic, continued openers, group limits and SLL/LL property replay 905,20261101; scripts/QualifyVoltageReferences.cs records named native syntax acceptance separately from numerical agreement and vendor-fragment observations. Signal references remain unsupported by ParameterEvaluator. The scaled LIMIT oracle control has unresolved numeric disagreement and is not a numerical pass. This requirement remains Draft; selected plain v references do not establish complete expression/dialect conformance or behavioral simulation support.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: PRS-LEX-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-TABLE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Context-specific controlled-source TABLE syntax
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall recognize the selected E/G controlled-source TABLE form with an expression, an optional equals separator and continued coordinate pairs, preserving source spelling and physical locations. Table syntax shall be recognized in its declared card context without relaxing ordinary expression assignment or delimiter validation. Structural recognition shall remain separate from table interpolation, numerical support and dialect-specific legacy grouping policy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Bounded implementation under verification: context-specific generated tableTail/tablePair rules with contextual keyword selection and source-form observations; TableSyntaxTests and QualifyTables.cs. Inferred from reached vendor-library diagnostics after PRS-REF-001: opa1611.lib line 408 onward, TLV6001.LIB line 297 onward, TLV9002.lib line 238 and OPA171.txt line 310 onward. Named native acceptance is tested separately from numerical agreement; legacy wrapper adjudication remains required before broader closure; MCP6041.txt non-balanced coordinate wrappers are qualified separately by PRS-TABLE-002; they are not ordinary expression groups. TL072.301 also retains a terminal DOS control-Z input-profile question. Do not label those vendor inputs invalid merely because the current generated grammar rejects them.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: PRS-LEX-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-TABLE-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Local legacy TABLE coordinate separators
STATEMENT: >>>
Within the selected E/G TABLE coordinate tail only, commas and parentheses shall act as scalar separators as in the pinned native ngspice compatibility reader. Legacy extra or unmatched coordinate wrappers shall not by themselves cause rejection. A table shall contain a nonempty even number of coordinates. Controlling expressions and expressions outside the coordinate tail shall retain their ordinary delimiter and operand requirements. Recognition shall not imply interpolation support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred from inpcom.c TABLE translation using gettok_node and executed native controls: both MCP6041 wrapper spellings and a missing terminal pair parenthesis complete ngspice operating points. Bounded implementation: tableCoordinate/tableSeparator/tablePair productions, TableSyntaxTests, and scripts/QualifyTables.cs. Native acceptance and numeric controls remain separate fields. Group/resource budgets still apply; no complete TABLE dialect qualification is claimed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: PRS-TABLE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PRS-EOF-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit terminal DOS end-of-file profile
STATEMENT: >>>
An explicitly qualified legacy fragment input profile shall recognize a terminal DOS control-Z marker without silently discarding interior content or changing original source locations. Interior control characters and content after a claimed end marker shall remain distinct malformed-input or unsupported-profile outcomes. Syntax acceptance shall remain separate from resource resolution and model execution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred unimplemented draft from TL072.301 line 43, the remaining rejection in the fourteen-file reached-library recognition profile after TABLE support. Native acceptance of terminal versus interior/trailed markers and platform behavior must be tested before implementation or closure. No generic control-character stripping is authorized by this draft.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: PRS-LEX-001
